Hmm, one more risk: the pane mounts, `setVisible(true,'chat')` fires BEFORE `attach()` — and the runtime's `setVisible` requires `this.attached`; if the viewport is still owned by... it's host-guarded. If viewportHost==='chat' already (transferring back from the hub) and attached===true with old bounds, this early call could re-show the view at the OLD bounds for a frame before the attach arrives. Minor, acceptable (the original code had the same via its own setVisible(true) path).

